\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f2\fs24\u-10178?\u-8736?\f1  \f0 Culture \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Merch MVP: System Overview\par
\par
This is a daily pipeline that:\par
\par
Pulls Reddit trends\par
\par
Scores viability\par
\par
Selects top 20 (quota balanced)\par
\par
Runs AI enrichment + commercial sniff test\par
\par
Generates:\par
\par
Tier 1 email (teaser)\par
\par
Tier 2 email (top 4 + PDF attached)\par
\par
Full HTML + PDF report\par
\par
JSON archive\par
\par
\f4\u-10179?\u-8959?\f1  \f0 High-Level Execution Flow (main.py \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 run())\par
\f2 1\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  Fetch Raw Trends (Cheap)\par
trends = get_reddit_trends()\par
\par
\par
Source: trends_reddit.py\par
\par
Pulls hot posts from:\par
\par
r/funny\par
\par
r/memes\par
\par
r/showerthoughts\par
\par
r/wholesomememes\par
\par
Filters obvious junk titles\par
\par
Returns list of dicts:\par
\par
\{\par
    "title": str,\par
    "subreddit": str,\par
    "score": int\par
\}\par
\par
\par
No AI yet.\par
\par
\f2 2\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  Score Viability (Rule-Based, Cheap)\par
for t in trends:\par
    t["viability"] = score_trend(t)\par
\par
\par
Adds:\par
\par
"viability": "High" | "Medium" | "Low"\par
\par
\par
Still no AI.\par
\par
\f2 3\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  Filter + Sort\par
trends = [\par
    t for t in trends\par
    if t["viability"] in ["High", "Medium"]\par
]\par
\par
trends.sort(key=lambda t: \{"High": 1, "Medium": 2\}[t["viability"]])\par
\par
\par
Now we have viable candidates only.\par
\par
\f2 4\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  Apply Subreddit Quotas + Lock TOP_N\par
TOP_N = 20\par
\par
\par
Quota-balanced selection:\par
\par
selected = [...]\par
\par
\par
At this point:\par
\par
selected = canonical list of 20 trends\par
This list feeds everything else.\par
\par
Nothing outside selected is allowed to hit AI.\par
\par
\f4\u-10179?\u-8923?\f1  \f0 From Here On: AI Only Touches selected\par
\f2 5\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  Tier-2 Commercial Sniff Test (AI)\par
\par
File: tier2_sniff.py\par
\par
trend["tier2_sniff"] = run_tier2_sniff(trend, client)\par
\par
\par
Returns structured JSON:\par
\par
\{\par
  "sniff_score": int (0-100),\par
  "verdict": str,\par
  "confidence": str,\par
  "explanation": \{\par
      "why_it_works": str,\par
      "main_risk": str,\par
      "who_it_resonates_with": str,\par
      "why_people_would_buy": str\par
  \}\par
\}\par
\par
\par
Only runs on the final 20.\par
\par
\f2 6\u-497?\f5\u8419?\f0  AI Enrichment (Design + Merch Angle)\par
\par
File: ai_insights.py\par
\par
ai_data = enrich_trend_with_ai(trend, prompt)\par
\par
\par
Attaches:\par
\par
trend["ai_enrichment"] = \{\par
    "merch_angle": str,\par
    "slogan": str,\par
    "design": list,\par
    "merch_fit": dict,\par
    "keywords": list,\par
    "risks": str,\par
    "trend_signals": dict\par
\}\par
\par
\f4\u-10179?\u-8980?\f1  \f0 Email Layer\par
\par
Before emailing, trends are normalized:\par
\par
email_trends = [\par
    normalize_trend_for_email(t)\par
    for t in selected\par
]\par
\par
Tier 1 Email\par
\par
AI-written summary\par
\par
Uses all 20\par
\par
No attachment\par
\par
generate_tier1_email(...)\par
send_tier1_email(...)\par
\par
Tier 2 Email\par
\par
Shows top 4\par
\par
Includes sniff score + verdict\par
\par
PDF attached\par
\par
generate_tier2_email(...)\par
send_tier2_email(...)\par
\par
\f4\u-10179?\u-9020?\f1  \f0 Report Generation\par
\par
HTML report built manually\par
\par
Saved to /output\par
\par
Converted to PDF via wkhtmltopdf\par
\par
Attached to Tier 2 email\par
\par
JSON archive saved for debugging\par
\par
\f4\u-10180?\u-8233?\f1  \f0 Architectural Rules\par
\par
Reddit fetch is ingestion only\par
\par
Viability scoring is deterministic + cheap\par
\par
AI only runs after TOP_N lock\par
\par
selected is the canonical source of truth\par
\par
Sniff test never runs on more than 20 trends\par
\par
Emails + PDF both derive from the same list\par
\par
